                <head>340. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On October 8, the Shah delivered his speech from the throne marking the
                    ceremonial opening of the Iranian Senate and declared Iran’s intentions of
                    joining the Baghdad Pact. On October 12, Prime Minister Ala presented the Senate
                    with a bill calling for ratification of Iran’s adherence to the Pact. On that
                    same day, Soviet newspapers in Moscow reported that Molotov had warned the
                    Iranian Chargé in Moscow that the Soviet Union attached serious significance to
                    Iran’s adherence to the Pact, which Molotov described as contrary to good
                    Soviet-Iranian relations and existing treaty relations. (Telegrams 603 and 622
                    from Tehran, October 8 and 12, and telegram 880 from Moscow, October 13;
                    Department of State, Central Files, 780.5/ 10–855, 780.5/10–1255, and
                    661.88/10–1355, respectively)</p>
            </div>
